---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

export const prerender = true;

const pageTitle = "Garment Customs Clearance Guide for Importers | SDF Clothing";
const pageDescription = "Complete guide to customs clearance for imported clothing. Required documents, HTS codes, duty rates, common delays, broker tips."

const schema = [
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "Article",
    "headline": pageTitle,
    "description": pageDescription,
    "author": { "@id": "https://sdfltd.com/#org" },
    "publisher": { "@id": "https://sdfltd.com/#org" },
    "url": "https://sdfltd.com/insights/customs-clearance-guide/",
    "mainEntityOfPage": "https://sdfltd.com/insights/customs-clearance-guide/"
  }
];
---

<BaseLayout title={pageTitle} description={pageDescription} schema={schema}>

  <div class="container" style="padding: 3rem 1.5rem 5rem;">

    <nav aria-label="Breadcrumb" style="margin-bottom: 2.5rem;">
      <p style="font-size: 0.72rem; color: #FFFFFF; letter-spacing: 0.1em; text-transform: uppercase;">
        <a href="/" style="color: #e00; text-decoration: none;">Home</a>
        <span style="margin: 0 0.5rem; color: #333;"> | </span>
        <a href="/insights/index" style="color: #aaa; text-decoration: none;">Insights</a>
        <span style="margin: 0 0.5rem; color: #333;"> | </span>
        <span style="color: #FFFFFF;">Garment Customs Clearance Guide</span>
      </p>
    </nav>

    <article>

      <header style="max-width: 760px; margin-bottom: 3rem; padding-bottom: 2rem; border-bottom: 1px solid #1a1a1a;">
        <span style="font-size: 0.62rem; letter-spacing: 0.25em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #e00; display: block; margin-bottom: 1rem;">Trade & Logistics</span>
        <h1 style="font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 4vw, 2.8rem); font-weight: 200; color: #fff; line-height: 1.2; margin-bottom: 1.25rem; letter-spacing: 0.01em;">
          Garment Customs Clearance Guide | Smooth Import Process
        </h1>
        <p style="font-size: 1rem; color: #aaa; line-height: 1.9; margin: 0;">
          Customs clearance is the process of getting goods through customs. Proper documentation and preparation prevent delays. This guide explains what you need for smooth garment imports.
        </p>
      </header>

      <h2 style="font-size: 0.78rem; font-weight: 400; margin: 0 0 1.25rem; color: #fff; letter-spacing: 0.05em; text-transform: uppercase;">Required Customs Documents</h2>
      <p style="color: #aaa; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">Commercial invoice is essential. It must include product description, quantity, value, and Incoterms. The value declared must match the actual transaction value.</p>
      <p style="color: #aaa; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">Bill of lading or air waybill proves shipment. It serves as receipt and contract of carriage. The carrier issues this document when goods are shipped.</p>
      <p style="color: #aaa; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom: 3rem;">Packing list details the shipment contents. It lists each carton, its contents, and weight. This helps customs verify the shipment matches documentation.</p>

      <h2 style="font-size: 0.78rem; font-weight: 400; margin: 0 0 1.25rem; color: #fff; letter-spacing: 0.05em; text-transform: uppercase">HTS Code Classification</h2>
      <p style="color: #aaa; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">HTS codes classify products for duty determination. Each garment type has a specific code. Correct classification ensures accurate duty calculation.</p>
      <p style="color: #aaa; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">T-shirts use HTS 6109 or 6110 depending on material. Dresses use 6104 or 6111. Pants use 6103 or 6203. The first two digits indicate the chapter, the next four indicate the heading.</p>
      <p style="color: #aaa; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom: 3rem;">Incorrect classification causes problems. Customs may reclassify and charge additional duty. Consult HTS code guides or customs brokers for accurate classification.</p>

      <h2 style="font-size: 0.78rem; font-weight: 400; margin: 0 0 1.25rem; color: #fff; letter-spacing: 0.05em; text-transform: uppercase">Duty Rate Determination</h2>
      <p style="color: #aaa; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">Duty rates vary by HTS code and country of origin. The HTS code determines the base rate. The country of origin may modify this rate through trade agreements.</p>
      <p style="color: #aaa; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">Bangladesh qualifies for duty-free access to many markets. The EU grants duty-free status under EBA. The US has preferential rates for certain categories.</p>
      <p style="color: #aaa; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom: 3rem;">Certificate of origin proves country of origin. This document is required to claim preferential duty rates. SDF Clothing provides certificates of origin for all shipments.</p>

      <h2 style="font-size: 0.78rem; font-weight: 400; margin: 0 0 1.25rem; color: #fff; letter-spacing: 0.05em; text-transform: uppercase">Country of Origin Documentation</h2>
      <p style="color: #aaa; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">Certificate of origin is issued by the exporting country. It certifies that goods were produced in that country. This document is essential for claiming trade preferences.</p>
      <p style="color: #aaa; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">For Bangladesh, the Export Promotion Bureau issues certificates of origin. The manufacturer applies for this document after production is complete.</p>
      <p style="color: #aaa; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom: 3rem;">Some countries require specific certificate formats. Form A is common for developing countries. Form EUR1 is used for EU preferences. Check your destination country requirements.</p>

      <h2 style="font-size: 0.78rem; font-weight: 400; margin: 0 0 1.25rem; color: #fff; letter-spacing: 0.05em; text-transform: uppercase">Common Clearance Delays</h2>
      <p style="color: #aaa; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">Incomplete documentation causes delays. Missing or incorrect documents require customs to request corrections. This adds days or weeks to clearance time.</p>
      <p style="color: #aaa; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">Random inspections may occur. Customs may select shipments for physical inspection. This is normal but adds time to the process.</p>
      <p style="color: #aaa; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom: 3rem;">Peak season congestion causes delays. During busy periods, customs processing slows. Plan shipments to avoid peak periods when possible.</p>

      <h2 style="font-size: 0.78rem; font-weight: 400; margin: 0 0 1.25rem; color: #fff; letter-spacing: 0.05em; text-transform: uppercase">Customs Broker Selection</h2>
      <p style="color: #aaa; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">Customs brokers handle clearance on your behalf. They prepare documentation, communicate with customs, and arrange delivery. A good broker prevents problems.</p>
      <p style="color: #aaa; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">Choose a broker with garment import experience. They understand HTS codes for clothing. They know duty rates and trade agreements. This expertise saves time and money.</p>
      <p style="color: #aaa; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom: 3rem;">Broker fees typically range from $100 to $300 per shipment. This is a small cost compared to the value of avoiding delays and errors.</p>

      <h2 style="font-size: 0.78rem; font-weight: 400; margin: 0 0 1.25rem; color: #fff; letter-spacing: 0.05em; text-transform: uppercase">Customs Clearance FAQ</h2>
      <p style="color: #aaa; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;"><strong>How long does customs clearance take?</strong> Standard clearance takes 1-3 days. Inspections may add 1-2 weeks. Incomplete documentation can cause weeks of delay.</p>
      <p style="color: #aaa; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;"><strong>Can I clear customs myself?</strong> Yes, but it is complex. Customs procedures vary by country. Professional brokers have expertise that saves time and prevents errors.</p>
      <p style="color: #aaa; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;"><strong>What happens if customs rejects my shipment?</strong> Customs may require re-export or destruction. This is rare with proper documentation. Work with your broker to resolve issues quickly.</p>
      <p style="color: #aaa; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;"><strong>Do I need to pay duty before clearance?</strong> Yes. Duty must be paid before customs releases goods. Your broker can arrange payment on your behalf.</p>
      <p style="color: #aaa; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;"><strong>Can duty be refunded?</strong> Yes, if you overpay due to error. Refund processes exist but are slow. Accurate classification and documentation prevent overpayment.</p>
      <p style="color: #aaa; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom: 3rem;"><strong>What if I import through multiple ports?</strong> Each port has its own customs authority. Your broker can handle multiple ports. Consistent documentation helps regardless of entry point.</p>

      <div style="text-align: center; padding: 2.5rem; border: 1px solid #1a1a1a; border-top: 0.6px solid #e00; background: #050505; margin-top: 3rem;">
        <p style="color: #fff; font-size: 1rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; font-weight: 300;">
          Need help with customs documentation for your imports? SDF Clothing provides all required export documentation including commercial invoices, packing lists, and certificates of origin.
        </p>
        <a href="/contact" style="display: inline-block; background: #e00; color: #fff; padding: 0.9rem 2.5rem; text-decoration: none; font-size: 0.72rem; letter-spacing: 0.15em; text-transform: uppercase; transition: background 0.2s;">
          Discuss Documentation ?
        </a>
      </div>

      <p style="font-size: 0.85rem; color: #aaa; margin-top: 1.5rem; line-height: 1.8;">
        For a complete overview of clothing manufacturers in Bangladesh | including shipping, documentation, and import procedures | read our <a href="/clothing-manufacturers" style="color: #e00; text-decoration: none;">complete clothing manufacturers guide</a>.
      </p>

    </article>

  </div>

    
    </BaseLayout>



